{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_18fe6001cca2424f948668de","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a complete understanding of the shipped behavior:\n\n**`operatorOwnedFields`** = `[\"assignee\", \"previous_assignee\"]`:\n- When the key exists on disk, on-disk value always wins over a differing incoming snapshot.\n- Unlike controller-owned counters, an incoming value may introduce a key absent on disk.\n- Exception for `assignee` only: an incoming empty string is always applied (deliverer's deliberate Failed/needs_input clear, spec 039), produces no guard decision and no log line.\n\n**`mergeBody`**:\n- Splits both bodies into preamble + ordered sections by `## ` heading.\n- An on-disk-only heading is preserved in place with its content.\n- A heading present in both is replaced in place by the incoming content (heading + content).\n- A heading present only in incoming is appended after the last on-disk section (in incoming order).\n- Preamble: incoming wins when it has any non-whitespace text; otherwise the on-disk preamble is preserved. So the on-disk preamble survives when the incoming body starts with a heading (no preamble); an incoming body with its own preamble replaces the on-disk preamble; a body with no `## ` heading at all is preamble-only on both sides, so incoming preamble-only body still replaces on-disk preamble-only body (since incoming preamble has non-whitespace text).\n- A bare `---` line is never a heading and is preserved unescaped (well, preserved in content verbatim — the \"unescaped\" is in the original content; note: `content sanitization` escapes `---` elsewhere, but splitBody treats it as regular content).\n- Both `\\n` and `\\r\\n` line endings tolerated.\n- Escalation sections: `containsEscalationSection` checks for `\\n## Trigger Cap Escalation\\n` in body. Since `mergeBody` preserves on-disk escalation sections in place, the dedup check still sees them and doesn't append duplicate